---
/**
 * t38 · Facet
 *
 * Facets cut twice as wide as they are deep, so the top and bottom edges
 * slope rather than turn a corner, and the light rakes in from the side to
 * catch them. The tail falls away at that same two-to-one slope, and the
 * palette is the deepest of the four: a grape body that pushes the white
 * face to nearly nine to one. The body is symmetric about x=16 — 22 rows, 28
 * across at its widest — and the tail is exempt from that, as it is in every
 * mark in the family. It is cut from the same silhouette rather than stuck
 * on the side of one, so a single keyline runs round the two of them and
 * there is no seam where they meet.
 *
 * The interior is not a flat fill. Eight surface tones are laid down as a
 * 5-pixel contour bevel that follows every facet: each pixel takes its tone
 * from the local surface normal against a light off (4, 7), and from how far
 * it sits from that light, so the highlight gathers on the facets nearest it
 * and falls away across the rest instead of ringing the whole rim evenly.
 * Facets turned away from the light fall two tones below the body colour.
 * Neighbouring pixels never skip a tone.
 *
 * The middle stays plain. The 8-wide md face with the compact smile sits on
 * the core tone with 7 rows of body air above it and 7 below, measured on
 * the body and ignoring the tail, and nothing is cleared behind it.
 *
 * 9 tones, all purple, and a white face at 8.59:1 on the core.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Facet">
